{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2148-01-04 19:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital tonight?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2148-01-04 19:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi… I woke up with that same stomach pain again. It’s the one I always get — feels like my stomach just stops working. I threw up a few times today, yellow stuff."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2148-01-04 19:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds like your usual gastroparesis flare. Any fever, chest pain, or shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2148-01-04 19:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, no fever or chest pain. Just the pain and nausea. It’s worse than yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2148-01-04 19:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. The ER team gave you fluids, anti-nausea meds, and some pain relief. You’re on IV fluids now to keep you hydrated. We’ll start with IV anti-nausea meds and adjust pain control as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2148-01-04 19:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay… I just want the nausea to stop. It’s so hard to talk when I feel like this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2148-01-04 19:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Totally understandable. We’ll give you some medication to help with that right away. Just rest — I’ll check back soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2148-01-05 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today? Any vomiting overnight?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2148-01-05 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi… I threw up once last night, but it was clear. The nausea’s a little better since the IV meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2148-01-05 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s progress. Your labs show your white blood cell count is high — 20.2 — but it’s been high before, so we think it’s chronic and not from an infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2148-01-05 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, they said that last time too. Is it dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2148-01-05 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not necessarily. A hematology consult reviewed it — they think it’s reactive, not a blood disorder. We’ll keep monitoring it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2148-01-05 08:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. What about my iron? I know I haven’t been taking those pills regularly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2148-01-05 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs confirm iron deficiency anemia. Your B12 and folate are also low. Since oral iron hasn’t worked, we’re starting IV iron — two doses, 125 mg each."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2148-01-05 08:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that help me feel less tired?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2148-01-05 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, over time. You’ll also get B12 and folic acid supplements. We’ll send prescriptions home so you can continue them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2148-01-05 08:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ll try to take them this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2148-01-05 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood cultures came back — no infection. Stool test was negative for C. diff. That’s good news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2148-01-05 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not food poisoning or anything like that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2148-01-05 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, it doesn’t look like it. Your symptoms still point to a gastroparesis flare, likely triggered by stress or diet, but we can’t always pinpoint the cause."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2148-01-05 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. My mom’s cancer came back — that’s been really hard."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2148-01-05 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m so sorry to hear that. Emotional stress can definitely worsen gastroparesis and pain. We’re continuing your usual meds — lorazepam, tramadol, and ondansetron."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2148-01-05 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel like the tramadol helps, but I worry about using it too much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2148-01-05 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re using it carefully and only as needed. Your team is aware of the risks. We’re also watching for side effects from your other meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2148-01-06 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’ve had no vomiting since yesterday — that’s great. We’d like you to try some clear liquids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2148-01-06 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m still a little nauseous, but I can try."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2148-01-06 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Start slow — sip ginger ale or broth. If you keep that down, we’ll advance to soft foods later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2148-01-06 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well with the liquids. How’s your stomach now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2148-01-06 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. I even ate a few crackers without throwing up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2148-01-06 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent progress. Your kidney function was a little off when you arrived — creatinine went up to 1.3 — but it’s back to 1.1 now, likely from dehydration."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2148-01-06 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I be worried about my kidneys?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2148-01-06 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at this time. It improved with fluids. But we’ll keep monitoring it, especially since you have diabetes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2148-01-06 12:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right, I need to watch that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2148-01-06 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did an abdominal X-ray today. It shows mild constipation, but nothing blocked or dilated. That could be contributing to your discomfort."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2148-01-06 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been reluctant to take more meds… I’m already on so many."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2148-01-06 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We won’t add anything new now, but your PCP might consider adjusting your iron or stool softeners later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2148-01-07 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve kept down solid food for over 24 hours — that’s a big milestone. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow if all goes well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2148-01-07 08:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great! What about my insulin? My sugars were high at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2148-01-07 08:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You needed less insulin here because you weren’t eating much. We’re sending you home on 40 units of Lantus at bedtime — lower than before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2148-01-07 08:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I should increase it as I eat more?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2148-01-07 08:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Monitor your blood sugar daily and work with your doctor to adjust the dose gradually."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2148-01-07 08:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And the IV iron — do I need more?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2148-01-07 08:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You received two doses here. Talk to your PCP about outpatient infusions if needed. We’ve sent prescriptions for B12 and folic acid — take those daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2148-01-07 08:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2148-01-07 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One more thing — your EKG in the ER showed a prolonged QTc over 500. We didn’t restart reglan because of that. Please follow up with your doctor to repeat the EKG."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2148-01-07 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2148-01-07 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can be, so we’re being cautious. It may be from some of your medications or electrolyte changes. Your primary doctor will evaluate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2148-01-08 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. Vital signs are stable, abdomen is soft, and labs are improving. We’re ready to discharge you home today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2148-01-08 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you so much. I feel so much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2148-01-08 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Keep taking your medications as prescribed, follow up with your PCP in a week, and call if nausea or pain returns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2148-01-08 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll make sure to get that EKG done."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2148-01-08 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Take care — and give your mom our best."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2148-01-08 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2148-01-08 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before you leave — any last questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2148-01-08 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’ve got everything. The discharge instructions are clear."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2148-01-08 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’ll send all your records to your primary care doctor. Feel better soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2148-01-08 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2148-01-08 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. See you at follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2148-01-08 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2148-01-08 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will be in with your prescriptions and discharge papers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2148-01-08 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2148-01-08 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re all set. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2148-01-08 10:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you again for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2148-01-08 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2148-01-08 10:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Bye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2148-01-08 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Goodbye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2148-01-08 10:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Take care."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2148-01-04 19:09:00",
    "admission_end": "2148-01-08 18:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of type 2 diabetes, gastroparesis, anxiety, and chronic abdominal pain was admitted for acute-on-chronic abdominal pain and vomiting, consistent with a gastroparesis flare. She was treated with IV fluids, anti-nausea medications, and pain control. Labs revealed iron deficiency anemia, low B12 and folate, and chronic leukocytosis, prompting IV iron and supplementation. Her kidney function improved with hydration. She tolerated oral intake within 48 hours and was discharged home in stable condition. Insulin was adjusted downward, and she was advised to follow up with her primary care provider for medication titration, EKG monitoring for prolonged QTc, and outpatient iron management.",
    "problems": [
      "Type 2 diabetes mellitus with diabetic autonomic (poly)neuropathy",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Body mass index [BMI] 45.0-49.9, adult",
      "Essential (primary) hypertension",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Long term (current) use of insulin",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Constipation, unspecified",
      "Iron deficiency anemia, unspecified",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified",
      "Other elevated white blood cell count",
      "Pain disorder exclusively related to psychological factors",
      "Essential (hemorrhagic) thrombocythemia",
      "Obesity, unspecified",
      "Somnolence",
      "Adverse effect of butyrophenone and thiothixene neuroleptics, initial encounter",
      "Adverse effect of benzodiazepines, initial encounter",
      "Adverse effect of selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors, initial encounter",
      "Adverse effect of other synthetic narcotics, initial encounter",
      "Adverse effect of other antiepileptic and sedative-hypnotic drugs, initial encounter",
      "Unspecified place in hospital as the place of occurrence of the external cause"
    ]
  }
}
